# Local secrets for `wrangler dev` — copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored) and fill.
# In staging/prod these are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME> --env <env>`.

# Audit + session sink (POST /v1/events → EU D1) + the admin read/write routes:
# APP_API_TOKEN=""   # trusted server bearer — gates the admin routes and POST /v1/events.
#                    # Server-side only; NEVER bundle it.
# IP_HASH_SALT=""    # salt for hashing IPs before storage (never a raw IP is stored)

# Announcements (GET /v1/announcements → Sanity). PROJECT_ID/DATASET go in wrangler.toml
# [vars] (public); the read token is a secret, needed only if the dataset is not public-read:
# SANITY_API_READ_TOKEN=""   # server-side Sanity read token (never shipped to clients)

# Clerk webhook (Svix) — verifies POST /v1/clerk-webhook (user.created/updated/deleted → user_profiles sync).
# From Clerk Dashboard → Webhooks → your endpoint → Signing Secret.
CLERK_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# GDPR email-fingerprint salt — DISTINCT per env, STABLE within an env, never rotated on a live env.
GDPR_FINGERPRINT_SALT=""

# At-rest PII encryption (AES-256-GCM) for data_requests (the replyable email + free-text
# message). Unset → those fields store plaintext (backward compatible; the read path decrypts
# either). Server-side only — never a public prefix.
# PII_ENCRYPTION_KEY=""

# Transactional email (erasure token/completion + Clerk email take-over). RESEND_API_KEY is
# a secret → set it here; unset → email sends no-op (never throw). The sender EMAIL_FROM now
# lives in wrangler.toml [env.*.vars] (no-reply@updates.indiecrafts.dev, one domain per env) —
# do NOT also set it here, or wrangler warns about a var/secret name clash.
# RESEND_API_KEY=""

# Marketing-email consent mirrors to Resend's global Contacts (no audience id — Resend
# renamed Audiences to Segments). RESEND_API_KEY unset → the mirror no-ops (store-only).

# No-login email-preferences token (GET/POST /v1/email-preferences + the RFC 8058 one-click
# unsubscribe route). Unset → those routes answer 503.
# EMAIL_PREF_SECRET=""
